---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';

// Orders per day for the first drop, counted from the store's order export (aggregated, no customer data).
const firstDrop = { start: 'Jun 25, 2021', end: 'Jul 4', orders: [1, 0, 0, 40, 4, 3, 1, 4, 2, 1] };
const peak = Math.max(...firstDrop.orders);
---

<Base
  title="DvzzPins · David Salazar"
  description="I ran DvzzPins, a pin brand: I took my sketches to finished products with a designer and a manufacturer, then launched them as drops that sold out."
  current="work"
>
  <div class="case">
    <header class="case-head">
      <div class="col">
        <h1 data-reveal>DvzzPins</h1>
        <p class="lede" data-reveal>
          A pin brand I ran on my own. I turned my sketches into finished products with a designer
          and a manufacturer, then launched them as drops that sold out.
        </p>
        <dl class="spec" data-reveal>
          <dt>What</dt>
          <dd>An online pin brand, December 2020 to October 2022.</dd>
          <dt>Role</dt>
          <dd>Founder and only operator. I owned the vision, the design brief, the production and every launch.</dd>
          <dt>Result</dt>
          <dd>Four designs sold out completely. The first drop took 40 orders in a single day, and the store shipped to 156 customers in 24 states.</dd>
        </dl>
      </div>
    </header>

    <section>
      <div class="col">
        <h2 data-reveal>From sketch to product</h2>
        <div class="runin">
          <p data-reveal>
            <strong>The vision.</strong> Every product started as my own sketch of a pin I wanted
            to exist.
          </p>
          <p data-reveal>
            <strong>The design.</strong> I worked with a designer to turn those sketches into
            finished artwork. My job was to brief them, review what came back and say what to
            change until it matched what I had pictured.
          </p>
          <p data-reveal>
            <strong>The product.</strong> A manufacturer made the designs real. Before anything
            was produced, I checked and approved a proof of each design: the size, colors, finish
            and quantity.
          </p>
          <p data-reveal>
            <strong>The launch.</strong> I released the pins as limited drops, managed inventory
            and answered customers.
          </p>
        </div>
        <p data-reveal>
          It is the same loop I use in analysis work: a clear brief, a check of the output against
          it, and approval only when it matches.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="band">
      <div class="col">
        <h2 data-reveal>How the drops landed</h2>
        <p data-reveal>
          The first drop landed on June 28, 2021. The store took 40 orders that day, a fifth of
          every order it would ever receive, and 48 in its first six days.
        </p>
        <div data-reveal>
          <div class="columns-chart" role="img" aria-label={`Orders per day from ${firstDrop.start} to ${firstDrop.end}: ${firstDrop.orders.join(', ')}`}>
            {firstDrop.orders.map((n) => (
              <span style={`height:${(n / peak) * 100}%`}>{n >= 10 && <em>{n}</em>}</span>
            ))}
          </div>
          <div class="columns-labels" aria-hidden="true"><span>{firstDrop.start}</span><span>{firstDrop.end}</span></div>
          <p class="figure-note">Orders per day, first drop.</p>
        </div>
        <ul data-reveal>
          <li>Later drops followed the same pattern, including 15 orders in a single day in February 2022.</li>
          <li>Four designs sold out completely.</li>
          <li>Orders came from 156 customers in 24 states, and 29 of them came back to order again.</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="actions" data-reveal>
          <a class="btn" href="/#work">Back to work</a>
          <a class="textlink" href="/#contact">Get in touch</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
